The first round of the election was held in on 22 January, although 32.7% of eligible voters had cast their vote during the advance voting period between 11 and 17 January.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.hs.fi/politiikka/Ennakkoon+%C3%A4%C3%A4nest%C3%A4neit%C3%A4+viime+vaaleja+enemm%C3%A4n+/a1305553576848|title=Ennakkoon äänestäneitä viime vaaleja enemmän|work=Helsingin Sanomat|publisher=Sanoma News|agency=Suomen Tietotoimisto|date=17 January 2012|language=fi|access-date=23 January 2012}}</ref> The overall voter turnout in the first round was 72.8%. In the second round, 36.6% of votes were cast during the advance voting period between 25 and 31 January.<ref>{{cite web|author=${when} |url=http://www.hs.fi/politiikka/Ennakko%C3%A4%C3%A4nestyksess%C3%A4+ly%C3%B6tiin+viime+vaalien+luvut/a1305554619175 |title=Ennakkoäänestyksessä lyötiin viime vaalien luvut – Presidentinvaalit – Politiikka |publisher=HS.fi |access-date=7 February 2012}}</ref> The overall turnout in the second round was 68.9%.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://192.49.229.35/TP2012K2/s/aanaktiivisuus/aanestys1.htm |title=Äänestysaktiivisuus |publisher=192.49.229.35 |access-date=7 February 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120208005528/http://192.49.229.35/TP2012K2/s/aanaktiivisuus/aanestys1.htm |archive-date=8 February 2012 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

Since no candidate received a majority of votes in the first round, a [[two-round system|runoff election]] was held on 5 February between Sauli Niinistö (37.0% of first round votes) and Pekka Haavisto (18.8% of first round votes).<ref name="round1-results">{{cite web |url=https://tulospalvelu.vaalit.fi/TP2012K1/s/tulos/lasktila.html |title=Presidentinvaali 22.1.2012 |publisher=[[Ministry of Justice (Finland)]] |website=tulospalvelu.vaalit.fi |trans-title=First round results |date=24 January 2012 |access-date=28 March 2019 |archive-date=6 May 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140506171425/http://tulospalvelu.vaalit.fi/TP2012K1/s/tulos/lasktila.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> Niinistö won the second round with 62.6% of the vote and was thus elected as president.<ref name="round2-results">{{cite web |url=https://tulospalvelu.vaalit.fi/TP2012K2/s/tulos/lasktila.html |title=Presidentinvaali 5.2.2012 |publisher=[[Ministry of Justice (Finland)]] |website=tulospalvelu.vaalit.fi |trans-title=Second round results |date=8 February 2012 |access-date=28 March 2019 |archive-date=29 April 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170429231628/http://tulospalvelu.vaalit.fi/TP2012K2/s/tulos/lasktila.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> The result of the second round was verified on 8 February.<ref name="round2-results"/>

