===Reactions===
;First round
Of the six candidates defeated on the first round, Väyrynen was the only one not to express his support for either of the second-round candidates. Soini and Essayah backed Niinistö, while Lipponen, Arhinmäki and Biaudet supported Haavisto.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.demari.fi/uutispaiva-demari/uutiset/uusimmat/5116-haavisto-niinisto-3-2-pudonneista-vain-vayrynen-panttaa-kantaansa |title=Haavisto-Niinistö 3-2: Pudonneista vain Väyrynen panttaa kantaansa|work=Demari|access-date=7 February 2012}}</ref>

[[Mikael Jungner]], the party secretary of the Social Democratic Party, said that he would not continue in his role due to the poor showing of Lipponen.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://yle.fi/uutiset/talous_ja_politiikka/2012/01/jungner_ei_hae_jatkokautta_3203468.html |title=Jungner ei hae jatkokautta|publisher=Finnish Broadcasting Company|access-date=7 February 2012}}</ref>

